---
source: crates/rune-config/tests/eval.rs
description: npm value import
expression: "redact(dir.path(), &error)"
---
cannot import `lodash` from [TMP]/rune.config.ts

rune evaluates this config with an embedded JavaScript engine, so npm packages and Node built-in modules do not exist at runtime.

what does work:
  - `import type { ... } from "lodash"` — type-only imports are erased before evaluation
  - a relative import of a file in this repository, such as `./scripts/helpers.ts`
  - `import { defineConfig } from "@gio-labs/rune"` — the one package rune supplies itself
  - `import { rune } from "@gio-labs/rune"` — then `rune.env`, `rune.platform`, `rune.isCI`
